# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
================================================================================
 RT REQUIREMENTS & TEST-CASE TRACEABILITY DASHBOARD
================================================================================

A single Plotly-Dash application that serves TWO dashboards from one port,
switchable with the top-level tabs:

    * "Requirements" tab  - reads the Requirements workbooks (one sub-folder per
      project) and draws the five requirement graphs
      (Distribution / Validation / Trace / ASIL / CAL).

    * "Test Case" tab     - reads the Test-Case workbooks under ``D:/Test_Cases``
      (one sub-folder per module, each a mini sub-tab) and draws NINE graphs
      (Status / Result / Test Case Type / Test Criteria / Valuation /
       Responsible User / ASIL / CAL / Regression Test).

Both tabs share the same generic machinery - the differences live entirely in a
small set of dataclasses (``Dimension`` and ``Domain``), which is what keeps the
code industrial-grade rather than copy-pasted.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 WHAT CHANGED IN THIS REVISION (and why it matters)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. SCALE / "stuck on loading" fix.  The previous design read *every* workbook on
   start-up.  With hundreds or thousands of files that blocked the UI and the
   graphs appeared to hang on "Loading...".  The DataStore is now **lazy**: it
   only *discovers* files on disk (cheap filename parsing, no reading) and then
   reads **only the handful of workbooks a given view actually needs**
   (<= 10 days, <= 10 weekly days, <= 10 monthly days).  Reads run in parallel
   and are cached by (mtime,size).  Ten thousand files on disk still means only
   ~10 reads per view - so no graph is ever stuck loading.

2. DATE FORMAT.  Workbook file names (and every x-axis label) now use
   ``DD-MON-YY`` - e.g. ``26-OCT-26``.  The old ``DD-MM-YYYY`` names still parse,
   so nothing breaks.

3. WEEKLY / MONTHLY are now SINGLE-DAY, not aggregates:
     * Weekly  -> the Saturday of each ISO week; if that Saturday has no file,
                  the Friday; if neither exists, that week is skipped.
     * Monthly -> the last available date in each calendar month.

4. "TEST CASE TYPE" graph added to the Test Case tab (column "Test Case Type":
   Manual = dark blue, Automated = light blue).

5. PER-BAR, PER-GRAPH "no data".  If a given workbook is missing the column a
   particular graph needs, ONLY that graph's bar for that date is drawn empty
   with a small "no data" note - every other graph, and every other date, is
   unaffected.

6. TOTAL COUNT printed on top of every bar, on BOTH tabs.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 USAGE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    python app.py                         # serve both dashboards on :8050
    python app.py --root PATH             # Requirements root folder
    python app.py --tc-root PATH          # Test-Case root folder
    python app.py --demo                  # write sample data under both roots
    python app.py --selftest              # run the internal logic assertions
    python app.py --rendercheck --demo    # PROVE the graphs render (headless)

Author : Cowork / Claude
License : MIT
================================================================================
"""

